 ### [Best Viewpoint Selection via Opacity Entropy](1121-best-viewpoint-selection-via-opacity-entropy.md)
-Best Viewpoint Selection via Opacity Entropy selects representative camera viewpoints in volume visualization by maximizing the visual information content of the rendered image. It solves the problem of identifying camera positions that reveal the most structural detail in a volume dataset, which is critical for tasks such as transfer function reconstruction and multi-view initialization. Unlike sibling methods that may rely on radiometric calibration or joint optimization of neural fields, this method specifically targets the geometric and density information encoded in the alpha channel of differentiable volume renders. It sets itself apart by using a differentiable entropy metric on the opacity values to guide gradient-based optimization of camera parameters.
